.TH XUR.STD.CLI 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.cli \- argument parsing and interactive prompts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::cli;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::cli
provides command-line argument parsing via pico-args and
interactive terminal prompts via inquire.
.SH ARGUMENT PARSING
.TP
.B cli::args() -> Args
Parse the program's command-line arguments into an
.B Args
handle.
.SS Args methods
.TP
.B contains(flag) -> bool
Whether
.I flag
(e.g.\&
.BR \(dq\-\-verbose\(dq )
is present. Consumes it.
.TP
.B option(name) -> Option<str>
The value of a named option (e.g.\&
.BR \(dq\-\-output\(dq ).
Consumes the flag and its value.
.TP
.B value(name) -> Result<str, str>
Like
.BR option ,
but returns an error if the option is missing.
.TP
.B subcommand() -> Option<str>
The first free argument, if it does not start with
.BR \- .
.TP
.B free() -> Result<[str], str>
All remaining free (non-flag) arguments.
.TP
.B remaining() -> [str]
All remaining arguments, including flags.
.TP
.B finish() -> Result<(), str>
Verify that all arguments were consumed. Returns an error naming
any unexpected arguments.
.SS Declarative parsing
.TP
.B cli::parse(specs) -> Result<record, str>
Parse arguments from a list of spec records. Each spec has a
.B name
and optional
.BR short ,
.BR kind
.RB ( \(dqflag\(dq ,
.BR \(dqoption\(dq ,
.BR \(dqpositional\(dq ),
and
.BR default .
.SH TABLE
.TP
.B cli::table(headers, rows)
Print a formatted table to stdout.
.I headers
is a list of column name strings;
.I rows
is a list of lists.
.SH PROMPTS
Interactive prompts that read from the terminal:
.TP
.B cli::prompt(message) -> str
Ask for free-text input.
.TP
.B cli::confirm(message) -> bool
Ask a yes/no question.
.TP
.B cli::select(message, options) -> str
Choose one from a list of options.
.TP
.B cli::multi_select(message, options) -> [str]
Choose one or more from a list.
.TP
.B cli::password(message) -> str
Read a password (input is hidden).
.TP
.B cli::editor(message) -> str
Open the user's editor and return the text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::cli;
use std::io;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let args = cli::args();
    let verbose = args.contains("--verbose");
    let output = args.option("--output");
    let files = args.free()?;
    args.finish()?;
    for file in files {
        io::println("processing: {}", file);
    }
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.io (7)
